+# =============================================================================
+# EXTRA AGGREGATE FACTORS  (raises K, the dimension of the priced-risk space)
+#
+# WHY: see voc_diagnosis/findings.md section B3. With K priced aggregate shocks and L
+# characteristic portfolios, the best Sharpe attainable inside the linear characteristic
+# span is SR_lin/SR* ~ sqrt(L/K). BGN/KP14 have K=2 and GS21 K=1, so 6 Fama factors
+# OVER-span the SDF and the population ceiling on any DKKM-over-FM advantage is 1.01-1.03x.
+# Raising K is the only lever that moves that ceiling.
+#
+# CONSTRUCTION (BGN): the SDF is log M = -r - 0.5|lambda|^2 - lambda'nu, and a project's
+# price depends on its loading b_s ONLY through the scalar lambda'b_s. So write
+#     b_s = (beta_s / sigma_z) * u  +  g_s ,      lambda = sigma_z * u,  u'g_s = 0
+# and every price, expected return, investment decision, Jstar, D(r) and the (beta_star,
+# scale) calibration is LITERALLY unchanged -- only the cross-firm covariance moves.
+# Total cash-flow variance is preserved by taking the g_s budget out of the idiosyncratic
+# remainder:  |g_s|^2 = OMEGA * sigmaj^2 * (1 - corr_zj^2).
+#
+# The g_s directions are smooth Fourier modes of an OBSERVABLE firm coordinate tau_i, with
+# mode amplitudes decaying as k^(-DECAY/2). The decay exponent is DKKM's Theorem 3 axis:
+# their APT calibration has eigenvalues ~ p^(-2) (no virtue of complexity), their AIPT
+# calibration ~ p^(-0.5) (virtue of complexity). Loadings must be smooth functions of an
+# observable, NOT a latent categorical -- otherwise no method can hedge them and the
+# horse race is vacuous (and if they were categorical, FM plus dummies would span them).
+#
+# N_EXTRA_FACTORS = 0 reproduces the published models EXACTLY: no extra random draws are
+# consumed, so the panel is bit-identical. Verified by
+# voc_diagnosis/refactor_checks/golden.py.
+# =============================================================================
+
+BGN_SIGMAJ_BAND = 0.1 * 0.3  # width of the idiosyncratic cash-flow band at
+                             # panel_functions_bgn.py:54. The 0.1 was hand-inserted (see
+                             # the "# added a factor of 0.1" comment that used to be there)
+                             # and leaves mean(1 - corr_zj^2) = 0.071, i.e. only ~7% of
+                             # log-cash-flow variance is non-systematic. That 7% is the
+                             # entire budget the extra-factor block can draw on, so this
+                             # knob gates whether N_EXTRA_FACTORS does anything at all.
+                             # sigmaj enters NO valuation object (verified: prices, Jstar,
+                             # D(r), the investment rule and (beta_star, scale) are all
+                             # sigmaj-free), so raising it is a pure covariance change.
+                             # Critics capped the multiplier at 1.25x the unscaled 0.3;
+                             # 1.75x gives cash-flow CV 121 and excess kurtosis 149.
+
+BGN_N_EXTRA_FACTORS = 0      # K - 1. 0 => published model. Try 20-40 (see findings.md B3).
+BGN_EXTRA_OMEGA = 0.75       # share of NON-systematic cash-flow variance moved to the
+                             # common block. Capped below 1 so idiosyncratic variance
+                             # stays strictly positive.
+BGN_EXTRA_DECAY = 1.0        # mode amplitudes ~ k^(-DECAY/2), so kernel eigenvalues
+                             # ~ k^(-DECAY). 0.5 = AIPT-like, 2.0 = APT-like.
+
+# NOTE: BGN currently has mean corr_zj = 0.958, i.e. only ~7% of log-cash-flow variance is
+# non-systematic, so the common block is capped at ~7% of cash-flow variance no matter what
+# OMEGA is. Widening the sigmaj band at panel_functions_bgn.py:54 (the hand-inserted 0.1)
+# is a prerequisite for this lever to bite. See findings.md section G.
+
 # =============================================================================
 # KP14 Model Parameters
 # =============================================================================
